            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "@aladyshev22@gmail.com you seemed to want this tinyxml2 wrap file.  Going forward can you please keep it updated?  Thanks!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Konstantin Aladyshev",
                        "email": "aladyshev22@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Kostr"
                    },
                    "message": "I was doing it as a part of https://github.com/openbmc/openbmc/issues/3993\n\nBut unfortunately I don't think I have the resources to maintain local meson build for all of the openbmc projects on a regular basis"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": ">  I don't think I have the resources to maintain\n\nThat's ok, but I don't either, so if we can't find anyone willing to support tinyxml2.wrap, the logical course of action would be to drop it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Fine with me to merge, or just leave at the previous version."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't think it really matters that much if people aren't jumping on pushing up commits as soon as new versions are released.  I guess the most likely thing is someone changes objmgr code so it doesn't work with the old version anymore, and either updates the wrap then or the next person that tries it would just fix it.\n\nThis isn't the only repo this file exists in.\n\nIf people really don't want this file, then how about the readme is updated to mention which package one's system would need installed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "> I don't think it really matters that much if people aren't jumping on pushing up commits as soon as new versions are released.\n\nIt isn't really the latency or that the release is older that concerns me here.  I pushed back on this when it was initially proposed because it is an unusual use-case...most people just install tinyxml2 development headers in their container or on their development host.  What does concern me is setting a precedent that we'll accept code in support of unusual use cases and maintain it forever for free.\n\n> If people really don't want this file\n\nI'm not in any hurry.  I thought I'd just ask a question to get a sense of how well this is going to be maintained."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks Matt."
                }
            ],
